---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../components/Disclaimer.astro';
import AuthorByline from '../components/AuthorByline.astro';
import { BUSINESS, MEDICARE_2026 } from '../data/site';

const title = `The ${MEDICARE_2026.year} High-Deductible Plan G Deductible, Explained`;
const description = `The 2026 High-Deductible Plan G deductible is ${MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible}. See exactly what counts toward it, how it works over a year, and when it resets.`;
const today = '2026-06-03';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is the High-Deductible Plan G deductible for 2026?', a: `It is ${MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} for ${MEDICARE_2026.year}. You pay Medicare-covered out-of-pocket costs yourself until you reach that amount; after that, the plan pays 100% of Medicare-approved charges for the rest of the calendar year. Medicare sets this figure and adjusts it each year.` },
  { q: 'Does the Part B deductible count toward the High-Deductible Plan G deductible?', a: `Yes. The Medicare Part B deductible (${MEDICARE_2026.partBDeductible} in ${MEDICARE_2026.year}) counts toward your ${MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} high-deductible amount — it is not an extra charge stacked on top.` },
  { q: 'Does the deductible reset every year?', a: 'Yes. The high-deductible amount resets at the start of each calendar year, on January 1. Spending from the previous year does not carry over.' },
  { q: 'What happens after I meet the deductible?', a: 'Once your covered costs reach the annual deductible, the plan works exactly like standard Plan G and pays 100% of Medicare-approved costs for the remainder of that calendar year.' },
];

const articleSchema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, description, author: { '@id': `${BUSINESS.url}/#agent` }, publisher: { '@id': `${BUSINESS.url}/#organization` }, datePublished: today, dateModified: today, mainEntityOfPage: `${BUSINESS.url}/high-deductible-plan-g-deductible-2026` };
const faqSchema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) };
const speakableSchema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `${BUSINESS.url}/high-deductible-plan-g-deductible-2026#webpage`, name: title, speakable: { '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification', cssSelector: ['.lead', 'h2'] } };
const schema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@graph': [articleSchema, faqSchema, speakableSchema] };
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <PageHero
    title={`The ${MEDICARE_2026.year} High-Deductible Plan G Deductible, Explained`}
    subtitle={`One number drives this whole plan: ${MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible}. Here’s what counts toward it and how it actually works.`}
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Medicare Plans', href: '/services' }, { label: 'High-Deductible Plan G', href: '/services/high-deductible-medicare-supplement' }, { label: `${MEDICARE_2026.year} Deductible` }]}
  />

  <div class="bg-crst-light border-b border-navy-100">
    <div class="container-wide py-3 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-2 sm:gap-4 text-center">
      <span class="text-sm font-heading text-navy-700">Questions about how the deductible would work for you?</span>
      <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneClean}`} class="btn-accent text-sm px-5 py-2">Call or text {BUSINESS.phone}</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="py-14 lg:py-18">
    <div class="container-narrow prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-crst-primary prose-a:text-crst-accent">

      <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-crst-gold bg-navy-50 p-5">
        <p class="text-navy-800 leading-relaxed m-0">
          The High-Deductible Plan G deductible for {MEDICARE_2026.year} is <strong>{MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible}</strong>. You pay
          the Medicare-covered costs the plan would normally cover — including the {MEDICARE_2026.partBDeductible} Part B deductible
          — out of pocket until your spending reaches {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible}. After that, the plan pays 100% of
          Medicare-approved costs for the rest of the calendar year. The amount resets every January.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="lead text-xl text-navy-700">
        Understanding this one number is the key to understanding the whole plan. It’s simpler than it looks.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-500 -mt-2">
        Written by <a href="/about">Jim Farnham, MS, MBA</a> — licensed independent agent (NY license {BUSINESS.nyLicense}).
      </p>

      <h2>What counts toward the deductible?</h2>
      <p>
        The costs that count are the ones the plan would otherwise pay on your behalf — the deductibles, copays, and coinsurance
        Original Medicare leaves to you. The Part B deductible counts toward the total, so it isn’t a separate, additional charge.
        As you use Medicare-covered care through the year, those out-of-pocket amounts add up toward your {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible}.
      </p>

      <h2>How the deductible works over a year</h2>
      <p>
        Think of it as a running tally. Early in the year, you pay your share of Medicare-covered costs yourself, and each payment
        moves you closer to the deductible. The moment your covered costs reach {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible}, the plan takes over and
        pays 100% of Medicare-approved charges for the rest of the year — just like standard Plan G. In a year where you use little
        care, you may never reach the deductible at all, and you simply keep the savings from the lower premium.
      </p>

      <h2>Does the Part B deductible count toward it?</h2>
      <div class="not-prose mb-5 rounded-lg bg-crst-light p-4">
        <p class="m-0 text-navy-800 leading-relaxed">
          Yes. The {MEDICARE_2026.year} Part B deductible of {MEDICARE_2026.partBDeductible} counts toward your
          {' '}{MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} high-deductible amount. It is not stacked on top.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>When does the deductible reset?</h2>
      <p>
        It resets at the start of each calendar year, on January 1. Whatever you spent toward the deductible last year does not
        carry forward. Medicare also adjusts the deductible amount annually, so the figure changes from one year to the next.
      </p>

      <h2>How the deductible affects whether the plan fits you</h2>
      <p>
        Because the deductible is a fixed, known number, it makes the math straightforward: your worst case in any year is your low
        premium plus {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible}. Whether that’s a good deal for you depends on how much care you expect to use — we
        walk through that in <a href="/high-deductible-plan-g-worth-it">Is High-Deductible Plan G worth it?</a>
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 rounded-xl bg-crst-primary p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-white font-heading text-lg mb-3 m-0">Want to see how the deductible plays out for your situation?</p>
        <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneClean}`} class="btn-accent text-base px-7 py-3">Call {BUSINESS.phone}</a>
      </div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      {faqs.map((f) => (<div class="mb-5"><h3 class="text-xl">{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></div>))}

      <p>
        For the full picture, start with the
        <a href="/services/high-deductible-medicare-supplement">guide to High-Deductible Plan G</a>, or compare it to
        <a href="/high-deductible-plan-g-vs-plan-g">standard Plan G</a>.
      </p>

      <AuthorByline />

      <div class="not-prose mt-8">
        <Disclaimer variant="tpmo" />
        <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          The {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} figure is the {MEDICARE_2026.year} High-Deductible Plan F/G deductible set by Medicare and
          changes annually. High-Deductible Plan G is not suitable for everyone. NY producer license #: {BUSINESS.nyLicense}.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          Source: <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/medigap" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Medicare.gov — Medicare Supplement (Medigap)</a> and the CMS annual deductible announcement.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <CTASection headline="Let’s talk through how the deductible would work for you" />
</BaseLayout>
